From 3275bd29f3a916b6a291084cd02a987bcceb5009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashwin Naik <ashwinnaik@google.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 05:20:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix memory leak in readspecs() during error handling.

The line buffer `l` allocated by `getln()` was not being freed when
the code jumps to the `err` label leading to an ASAN memory leak.
This patch adds the missing `free(l)` call to ensure proper memory cleanup.

Bug: b/510970516
---
 lib/libpaper.c.in.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/lib/libpaper.c.in.in b/lib/libpaper.c.in.in
index 02af84a..46f9d34 100644
--- a/lib/libpaper.c.in.in
+++ b/lib/libpaper.c.in.in
@@ -267,6 +267,7 @@ static int readspecs(struct paper **papers_list, const char *specsfile, struct p
             } else
                 ret = PAPER_MISSING_FIELD;
         err:
+            free(l);
             free(wstr);
             free(hstr);
             free(ustr);
--
